  "topic_en": "Product (factor) decompositions of theta-type series with complex arguments (combinations with i), derived from the Jacobi triple product identity, and the resulting identities for sums of squares and quotients of such series.",
  "transcription": "Lit. J.\n\nAus 28 + i 30 folgt\n[46] $\\{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-\\}+i\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}\\} = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots \\frac{1+i}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}+ix^{\\frac{25}{8}}+ix^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{121}{8}}+$\nNun findet man aus 6 nach dem wie zwischen 22 u 23 gezeigt ist\n$(1+x^4y)(1+x^{10}y)(1+x^{16}y)\\ldots(1+\\frac{xx}{y})(1+\\frac{x^8}{y})(1+\\frac{x^{14}}{y})\\ldots(1-x^6)(1-x^{12})\\ldots$\n$= 1+\\frac{xx}{y}+x^4y+\\frac{x^{10}}{yy}+x^{14}yy+$\nAlso\n$(1+x^4i)(1-x^{10}i)(1+x^{16}i)\\ldots(1-\\frac{xx}{i})(1+\\frac{x^8}{i})(1-\\frac{x^{14}}{i})\\ldots(1+x^6)(1-x^{12})(1+x^{18})\\ldots$\n$=(1+ixx+ix^4+x^{10}+x^{14}+ \\&c.)$\nDaher die Zerlegungen in Factoren\n[47] $(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-)-i\\{1-2x+2x^4\\ldots\\} = (1-x)(1-x^3)(1-x^5)\\ldots(1-i)(1+x^3)(1-x^6)(1+x^9)\\ldots(1+ix)(1+ixx)(1-ix^4)(1-ix^5)$ {+$((1+ix^7)(1+ix^8)\\ldots$+}\nund ferner\n[48] $(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-)+i\\{1-2x+2x^4\\} = (1-x)(1-x^3)(1-x^5)\\ldots(1+i)(1+x^3)(1-x^6)(1+x^9)\\ldots(1-ix)(1-ixx)(1+ix^4)(1+ix^5)\\ldots$\n[49] $(1+2x^3+2x^{12}+)-i(1+2x+2x^4) = (1+x)(1+x^3)(1+x^5)\\ldots(1-i)(1-x^3)(1-x^6)(1-x^9)\\ldots(1+ix)(1+ixx)(1-ix^4)(1+ix^5)\\ldots$\n[50] $(1+2x^3+2x^{12}+)+i(1+2x+2x^4) = (1+x)(1+x^3)(1+x^5)\\ldots(1+i)(1-x^3)(1-x^6)(1-x^9)\\ldots(1+ix)(1-ixx)(1+ix^4)(1-ix^5)\\ldots$\nAlso aus der Multiplication von 47 u. 48\n[51] $(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-)^2+(1-2x+2x^4-) = 2(1-x)^2(1-x^3)^2(1-x^5)^2\\ldots(1+x^3)^2(1-x^6)^2(1+x^9)^2\\ldots(1+xx)(1+x^4)(1+x^8)(1+x^{10})\\ldots$\n$=2(1-x)^2(1-x^3)^2(1-x^5)^2\\ldots(1+x^3)^2(1+x^9)^2\\ldots(1-x^6)^2(1-x^{12})^2\\ldots(1+xx)(1+x^4)(1+x^6)(1+x^8)\\ldots$\n$=\\frac{2[x]^2\\,[x^6]^4\\,[x^6]^3\\,[x^4]}{[xx]^2\\,[x^3]^2\\,(x^{12})^2\\,[x^4]\\,[xx]} = \\frac{2[x]^2.[x^4][x^6]^7}{[x^2]^3[x^3]^2[x^{12}]^3}$\nUnd aus der Multiplication von 49 u 50\n[52] $(1+2x^3+2x^{12}+)^2+(1+2x+2x^4+)^2 = 2(1+x)^2(1+x^3)^2(1+x^5)^2\\ldots(1-x^3)^2(1-x^6)^2(1-x^9)^2\\ldots(1+xx)(1+x^4)(1+x^8)(1+x^{10}$\n$=\\frac{2[xx]^4\\,[x^3]^2\\,[x^4]\\,[x^6]}{[x]^2[x^4]^2\\,[xx]\\,[x^{12}]} = \\frac{2[xx]^3[x^3]^2[x^6]}{[x]^2[x^4].[x^{12}]}$\nund der Quotient\n[53] $\\frac{(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-)^2+(1-2x+2x^4-)^2}{(1+2x^3+2x^{12}+)^2+(1+2x+2x^4+)^2} = \\left(\\frac{1-x}{1+x}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{1-x^3}{1+x^3}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{1-x^5}{1+x^5}\\right)^2\\ldots\\left(\\frac{1+x^3}{1-x^3}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{1+x^9}{1-x^9}\\right)^2\\ldots = \\left(\\frac{1-x}{1+x}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{1-x^5}{1+x^5}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{1-x^7}{1+x^7}\\right)^2\\ldots$\n$=\\frac{[x]^4\\,[x^4]^2\\,[x^6]^6}{[x^2]^6\\,[x^3]^4\\,[x^{12}]^2}$",
